# Normalise line endings for text files regardless of a contributor's
# `core.autocrlf` setting, and mark bundled binary assets explicitly so
# Windows checkouts (where autocrlf defaults to true) never attempt CRLF
# translation on them. Git's own binary heuristic usually catches these, but
# a compact WAV encoding is not guaranteed to contain a NUL byte in the
# sampled region, so it is not something to rely on for audio assets that
# have to play back byte-for-byte.
* text=auto eol=lf

*.ttf binary
*.wav binary
*.png binary
*.ico binary
*.icns binary
